Z||000008||TI_3VOM||09-03-2001||10:33 PM||||The Fiero, 80's alternative music (yep, includes The Smiths, as well as The Alarm, Echo & The Bunnymen, Ministry, Front 242, early R.E.M., New Order, Jonny Kleg, and labels such as TVT Records and Wax Trax Records), Crime Story (thank you A&E for re-running them), Robotech (ok...so I'm an Anime nerd), British TV imports (Doctor Who, Dave Allen At Large, Monty Python's Flying Circus), the '85 Bears, Top Gun, and Gummi Bears.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||09-03-2001||10:38 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>...Of course - The death of Disco!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>AMEN, brotha!<P>I liked Sixteen Candles and The Breakfast Club. And Fast Times...<BR>  Spoken from amidst the smoldering wreckage of Washington's Z-28:<BR>"My father is a television repairman. He has the <I>ultimate</I> set of tools. We can fix it!!" -Jeff Spicoli<P>DEVO. Talking Heads. King Crimson's later stuff. Art music and Punk music, in general. <BR>Hair bands, with a few exceptions, didn't do a whole lot for me.<BR>I liked the stuff that *didn't* get played to death on the radio.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
