Z||000011||Jaygee79||09-03-2001||10:46 PM||||my favorite thing back then was New Kids On The Block  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>of course, I was only 11 at the time<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ranger Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||09-03-2001||10:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TI_3VOM:<BR><B>Raydar,<BR>   Did you ever hear of a hair band parody song called "Living On My Hair?" (same beat as that Bon Jovi song)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL! Nope. Wish I had.<P>I *did* hear a parody of Rod Stewart's "Do Ya' Think I'm Sexy?" done by a DJ named Steve Dahl (I think), called "Do Ya' Think I'm Disco?" <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||baldlobo||09-03-2001||11:00 PM||||transformers, M.A.S.K, captian power, smurffs, and some other stuff I can't remember(what do you expect from a kid born in the 80's).||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||09-03-2001||11:11 PM||||Hmm, the return of performance to the automotive industry (the 75-81 were bleak years, performance-wise).  Bruce Springsteen, Miami Vice, any John Hughes flick, but especially Some Kind of Wonderful, a young and nubile Lea Thompson (yum), the collaboration of Jerry Bruckheimer and Don Simpson (Top Gun, et al), definately early alternative music (punk got more widespread, as well).  Of course, I'm a child of the 80's as it were - Class of '83!  Gods, my 20th high school reunion is only in 2 years!  I gotta find a job!||||reg||6
Z||000015||Pontiaddict||09-04-2001||01:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Spoken from amidst the smoldering wreckage of Washington's Z-28:<BR>"My father is a television repairman. He has the <I>ultimate</I> set of tools. We can fix it!!" -Jeff Spicoli<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Does that part remind you of Tom Mentz, driver of the Goldberg Monster Truck? They even talk the same.<P>My faves From the 80's were...<BR>Pontiacs<BR>EFI<BR>Transformers. I never had the Fiero, but back then my favorite was the stock car.<BR>Voltron  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>While I wasn't a fan of the hair bands, their music was pretty good, for the most part.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaygee79:<BR><B>my favorite thing back then was New Kids On The Block   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>of course, I was only 11 at the time<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wouldn't that have been from the '90's?||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jaygee79||09-04-2001||08:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B> Wouldn't that have been from the '90's?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, they broke up in 92 I think.  It was very early 90s that I went to a concert, but they were mostly the 80s.||||reg||1
