Z||000024||banditbalz||09-04-2001||10:35 PM||||When I think back to the 80's I remember Billy Idol concerts, Miami Vice on Friday nights, the convergence of home computers, 5.0L Mustangs, The "Roxy" nightclub, "Black Label" beer, leather jackets, Depeche Mode, Sega video games, Pontiac Fieros, desert boots, Long island ice tea, Honda CRX's, Rubic's cube, The cult, and long days in highschool/college...<P>Yep, I grew up in the eighties!<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000025||artherd||09-05-2001||05:15 AM||||The Music<BR>The Movies<BR>The Dreams<BR>The Cars <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And me! (born 10-09-80, it counts backwards, cool!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000026||loafer87gt||09-05-2001||01:23 PM||||The 80's were a perfect time for a young boy to grow up in. My days use to packed with building legos listening to Frankie Goes to Hollywood, The Fixx, Falco, and other old 80's pop, and my evenings were spent watching such greats as Automan, The Manimal, Knight Rider, and the A-Team. THose were the days.||||reg||1
Z||000027||loafer87gt||09-05-2001||01:28 PM||||BTW guys, if you want to grab a whole load of great 80's music, goto <A HREF="http://www.radiohifi.com/80s.asx" TARGET=_blank>www.radiohifi.com/80s.asx</A>  It is a streaming radio station, but if you have a download  program such as Download accelerator plus, it will grab the days radio programming so you can save it to you harddrive. I grabbed over 400+ songs in one day!!!||||reg||1
Z||000028||kslish||09-05-2001||01:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>my evenings were spent watching such greats as Automan, The Manimal, Knight Rider, and the A-Team. THose were the days.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"One man can make a difference, Michael." <P>Ahh...yes, Knight Rider.  I actually have the original episode on VHS.  <P>David Hasselhoff is actually bringing Knight Rider back next year on TV as his next project since Baywatch got canned.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Joe Torma||09-05-2001||02:05 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kslish:<BR><B> David Hasselhoff is actually bringing Knight Rider back next year on TV as his next project since Baywatch got canned.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't do that to me...Are you sure???!!!!<P>80s stuff I like...<BR>*Definetely the music...esp New Order(they have a new single out, and an album soon   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<BR>*Knight Ryder<BR>*Matlock<BR>*Remember REAL Saturday Morning cartoons.  Smurfs,Garfield,Snorks,etc.<BR>*Goonies,Ghostbusters...there were lots of great movies.<BR>*My Commodore 64<P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">    <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||kslish||09-05-2001||04:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Don't do that to me...Are you sure???!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>TV Times (June 28, 2001):<P>DAVID GETS HIS KITT ON<P>Former Baywatch hunk David Hasselhoff recently told Entertainment Weekly that Michael Knight is coming out of retirement, hiring a couple of kids, and bringing an updated version of KITT the talking car back to battle criminals. <P>Hasselhoff is planning to revive his crime-fighting hero Michael Knight from the Eighties hit show Knight Rider. David revealed that his permed character has been frozen for the past 10 years after being poisoned. Once<BR>defrosted, Michael goes to work for a new organization run by the great-great-grandniece of his former boss Devon, also named Devon. And yes, KITT fans, the talking car will also return. 'Devon and her new partner will team up with the original Michael Knight and the new KITT car to carry Knight Rider into the future' says David.<P>The original voice of KITT, Screen Actors Guild President William Daniels, has already committed to the project. His credits also include portraying a teacher on Boy Meets World and an acerbic doctor on St. Elsewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000031||annieL||09-05-2001||06:28 PM||||The best part of the eighties was the music. And I know someone already posted something about Saturday morning cartoons but he (accidently?) omitted Fat Albert. <BR>In Jersey there are at least 3 radio stations that play 80's music!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000032||Urchin||09-05-2001||07:34 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kslish:<BR><B> TV Times (June 28, 2001):<P>DAVID GETS HIS KITT ON<P>Former Baywatch hunk David Hasselhoff recently told Entertainment Weekly that Michael Knight is coming out of retirement, hiring a couple of kids, and bringing an updated version of KITT the talking car back to battle criminals. <P>Hasselhoff is planning to revive his crime-fighting hero Michael Knight from the Eighties hit show Knight Rider. David revealed that his permed character has been frozen for the past 10 years after being poisoned. Once<BR>defrosted, Michael goes to work for a new organization run by the great-great-grandniece of his former boss Devon, also named Devon. And yes, KITT fans, the talking car will also return. 'Devon and her new partner will team up with the original Michael Knight and the new KITT car to carry Knight Rider into the future' says David.<P>The original voice of KITT, Screen Actors Guild President William Daniels, has already committed to the project. His credits also include portraying a teacher on Boy Meets World and an acerbic doctor on St. Elsewhere.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I know this slightly off topic, but on the Knight Rider note... does anyone remember KITT's enemy that appeared in a couple of episodes...KARR I believe was the name... Just curious<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
