Z||000034||MsBeth||09-05-2001||10:56 PM||||My boys ...one born in 84 and the other in 85,  all the old alternative music from the 80s- the smiths, omd, benjamin orr, some ABC, U2, Peter Gabriel and there's a song "Generals and Majors" can't remember who but love that song!  Movies- Ferris, Some Kind of Wonderful, The Breakfast Club oh and that one with John Cusak and Ione Skye, Pretty in Pink blah blah blah ...  <P>Clubbing, drinking, dancing - my old job at Blue Cross.  Oh I do miss the 80s  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blue_2.gif">  <P>MsBeth||||reg||7
Z||000035||Tabs||09-05-2001||11:06 PM||||my top 10 favs 80's things<P>10.I was born in 1981<BR>9. Alf<BR>8.Big hair rock bands<BR>7.The Breakfast Club<BR>6.Back To The Future<BR>5.Who's The Boss<BR>4.Batman 1989<BR>3.Torn Jeans<BR>2.The Fiero<BR>And numbers 1 is.................<BR>Prince/The Artist or 0(+&gt;<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000036||TI_3VOM||09-05-2001||11:16 PM||||Ms Beth,<BR>   Generals and Majors was sung by XTC. Love that group (& they're still around, making music). Glad to see some of those groups still around. New Order just released a new album (after an 8 year vacation). The Cure is about to release a greatest hits collection (supposedly with a few new songs). Siouxie Sioux and Budgee (of Siouxie & the Banshees) are still around (under the moniker of Creatures). Depeche Mode and Ministry had releases earlier this year. Ian McCulloch reunited with The Bunnymen, bringing back Echo & The Bunnymen (FYI, Ian is not Echo...that's the name the group gave their drum machine). <BR>Ahhh.....Memories....."sniff"||||reg||1
Z||000037||MsBeth||09-06-2001||06:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TI_3VOM:<BR><B>Ms Beth,<BR>   Generals and Majors was sung by XTC. Love that group (& they're still around, making music). <BR>Ahhh.....Memories....."sniff"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OMG XTC ... racked my brain for 10 mins before I posted - and then it took me forever to get sleep because I couldn't remember-thanks.  No way Creatures you say - I love Siouxie, I will have to look around for the new stuff!  Looking forward to the Cure,  and will also have to look for the new stuff from Depressed Mode  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> and Ministry - thanks for the heads up on these - memories is right - thanks again!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blue_2.gif">  <P>MsBeth||||reg||1
Z||000038||TI_3VOM||09-06-2001||12:56 PM||||MsBeth,<BR>   No prob, and my pleasure. (always interested in helping a fellow 80's alt. music fan). If you (and anyone else) like to listen to New Order, then go to <A HREF="http://www.neworderonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.neworderonline.com</A>   or go to <A HREF="http://www.neworderweb.com" TARGET=_blank>www.neworderweb.com</A>    Lots of music to listen to.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000039||thomas_l||09-06-2001||01:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>   *Remember REAL Saturday Morning cartoons.  Smurfs,Garfield,Snorks,etc.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sheesh! Now I feel old. "Real" cartoons to me were like Wile E. Coyote and Foghorn Leghorn. Or Johnny Quest and Speed Racer. When those purple things came on TV I would rather be outside cleaning garbage cans or something. Bah.||||reg||13
