Z||000042||WampusCat||09-06-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tabs:<BR><B>my top 10 favs 80's things<P>10.I was born in 1981<BR>9. Alf<BR>8.Big hair rock bands<BR>7.The Breakfast Club<BR>6.Back To The Future<BR>5.Who's The Boss<BR>4.Batman 1989<BR>3.Torn Jeans<BR>2.The Fiero<BR>And numbers 1 is.................<BR>Prince/The Artist or 0(+&gt;</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I always thought the ALF cartoons on Sat. morning were much funnier and more intelligently written than the primetime series.  Lots of social commentary that must have been aimed over the heads of the kids.||||reg||1
Z||000043||Indyellowgt||09-07-2001||10:25 PM||||HOLD THE PHONE!!!<BR>You guys forgot to mention:<BR>Atari,<BR>Intellivision,<BR>Colecovision,<BR>High-top sneakers,<BR>And Garbage Pail Kids.Remember THOSE!!??<BR>I have a whole box of those things still!<BR>I LOVE the 80's.That is why I STILL have such a HUGE and further growing passion for our great Fiero.<BR>I remember New years eve,'80.<BR>I was almost 4,and all I really remember was my mom crying(she *always*cries at the turn of the decade..you should of seen her eve 0f 2000...Oh-Boy..)Anyway...Disco was still king,and there was always these terrible "dance shows" on at like 8pm every night,you know the ones...with the Michal Jackson lighting up floor as they danced??.LAME.<BR>WOW,I'm glad all that stuff has fizzled out,but the one thing that remains not out of date is the fiero.Ahh...Heaven.I remeber in '84/85 when GM had that lawsuit against Toyota for the MR2.I can't remeber what it was all about,but I remember thinking,"That's it,when I grow up I want a Fiero."And The Fiero WAS my very first car.<BR>You know,if you look at an 86GT fastback..just think how GOOD it looks.Then fill in what other domestic auto makers had to offer(as far as looks).Dodge had the K-car,ford had the EXP..HAHAHAHAHAHAHA.<BR>Ummm..anyway,enough reminicing,I'm going to go put on some Hall and Oats 45's and cry into my Pepsi Free......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Mark||||reg||4
Z||000044||MsBeth||09-08-2001||12:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TI_3VOM:<BR><B>MsBeth,<BR>   No prob, and my pleasure. (always interested in helping a fellow 80's alt. music fan). If you (and anyone else) like to listen to New Order, then go to <A HREF="http://www.neworderonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.neworderonline.com</A>   or go to <A HREF="http://www.neworderweb.com" TARGET=_blank>www.neworderweb.com</A>    Lots of music to listen to.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks! <P>MsBeth||||reg||1
